I am an OE user as well, so bear with me.

OE is a mail program. Not a very good one, but it is. It can also read
and send posts.

When reading posts, OE "recognises" lines beginning with "begin ...",
and thinks these indicate attachments. You'll notice that David's
messages show the paperclip in the upper right corner of your preview
window.

Since the "begin quoting" line does not mention a attachment type that
OE recognises (UUE, MIME, or something like that), OE doesn't know how
to display the "attachment" (which actually is plain ASCII text). Hence,
no attachment is shown at all, even if you try to open it.

The only way to show the attachment is to right-click on the message (in
the message list), choose "properties" (or whatever that is called in
your own language), choose the "details" tab, and click on "message
source".

A lot of work, and very annoying.

